# Phaser Error Handling Standards

## Description

Establishes standards for error handling, logging, and debugging in Phaser games to ensure consistent error management and recovery.

## Rule

1. Error Types:
   - MUST define custom error types:

     ```typescript
     export class GameError extends Error {
       constructor(message: string, public readonly code: string) {
         super(message);
         this.name = 'GameError';
       }
     }

     export class AssetError extends GameError {
       constructor(message: string) {
         super(message, 'ASSET_ERROR');
         this.name = 'AssetError';
       }
     }

     export class SceneError extends GameError {
       constructor(message: string) {
         super(message, 'SCENE_ERROR');
         this.name = 'SceneError';
       }
     }
     ```

2. Error Handling:
   - MUST implement error recovery:

     ```typescript
     export class ErrorHandler {
       static handle(error: Error, scene: Phaser.Scene): void {
         if (error instanceof AssetError) {
           // Handle missing or corrupt assets
           scene.scene.start('error-scene', { 
             message: 'Failed to load game assets',
             retry: true 
           });
         } else if (error instanceof SceneError) {
           // Handle scene initialization failures
           scene.scene.start('menu-scene');
         } else {
           // Handle unknown errors
           console.error('[GameError]', error);
           scene.scene.start('error-scene', { 
             message: 'An unexpected error occurred',
             retry: false 
           });
         }
       }
     }
     ```

3. Debug Logging:
   - MUST use structured logging:

     ```typescript
     export class GameLogger {
       static log(level: 'info' | 'warn' | 'error', message: string, data?: any): void {
         if (!process.env.DEBUG) return;

         const timestamp = new Date().toISOString();
         const logData = {
           timestamp,
           level,
           message,
           ...data
         };

         console.log(`[${level.toUpperCase()}] ${JSON.stringify(logData)}`);
       }

       static error(error: Error, context?: any): void {
         this.log('error', error.message, {
           name: error.name,
           stack: error.stack,
           ...context
         });
       }
     }
     ```

4. Scene Error Recovery:
   - MUST implement error boundaries:

     ```typescript
     export class ErrorBoundaryScene extends Phaser.Scene {
       private errorCount: number = 0;
       private readonly MAX_RETRIES: number = 3;

       create(): void {
         try {
           this.setupScene();
         } catch (error) {
           this.handleSceneError(error);
         }
       }

       private handleSceneError(error: Error): void {
         this.errorCount++;
         
         if (this.errorCount >= this.MAX_RETRIES) {
           ErrorHandler.handle(error, this);
         } else {
           GameLogger.error(error, { retryCount: this.errorCount });
           this.scene.restart();
         }
       }

       protected abstract setupScene(): void;
     }
     ```

